# Project copies of Cursor plans

When you create or update a plan (CreatePlan, plan mode, or a `.plan.md` file):

1. Write or copy it to **`.cursor/plans/` in this repo**, not only the user home Cursor plans directory (for example `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\plans\`).
2. Keep the home copy if Cursor writes one; the repo copy is required in addition.
3. Use a stable kebab-case name such as `paired_analysis_workflow.plan.md`.
4. Set `isProject: true` on the repo copy.
5. If you later revise the plan, update the repo file in the same turn.

Do not put plans under `.cursor/plans/` in the home folder only and leave the project without a copy.
